---
title: Hot rooms
---
On a map of rooms, the route says which rooms a player has to pass through and which are optional [[t:267-269 s:30]].

## The rule
1. Find the route from the start to the exit [[c21:131]].
2. Test every step of the route against each room, grown by one row [[c21:132-141]].
   - **In effect,** when the talk’s code is run: a step on any tile of the room except its last column. {{talk.c21.notLastColumnRule}} exceptions among {{talk.c21.rooms}} rooms on seeds 0 to 199 [[run:talk.c21.notLastColumnRule talk.c21.rooms]].
   - **Why the extra row:** the library’s test skips a rectangle’s last row and last column, but a room is drawn with both. The extra row restores the last row; the last column stays untested [[own]].
   - **Ours:** the same test [[own]].
3. Highlight the rooms on the route, and gray the rest [[c21:131-154]].

- **Talk says,** of the gray rooms: cull them for a room-to-room game, or hide bonus things in them [[t:269-271]].
- **Talk says,** of the rooms on the route: order a story along them, since the player will probably pass through them in order [[t:274-276 s:31]].

